<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oswaldo López Arellano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/2010">2010</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oswaldo López Arellano (1921–2010) was a Honduran air force officer who seized power in a coup in October 1963 against President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-villeda-morales">Ramón Villeda Morales</a> and dominated Honduran politics until 1975. He ruled from 1963 to 1971, a period that included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/football-war">Football War</a> with El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> in 1969, and again after a second coup from 1972. He was ousted in April 1975 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bananagate">Bananagate</a> bribery scandal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oswaldo-lopez-arellano.jpg" alt="Oswaldo López Arellano" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UPI Photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oswaldo_L%C3%B3pez_Arellano_in_1965.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Ramón Villeda Morales, president from 1957 to 1963, introduced a labour code, social security and a modest agrarian reform, but was overthrown in October 1963 by Colonel <b>Oswaldo López Arellano</b>, who dominated politics until 1975, when he fell over the ‘Bananagate’ scandal of bribes paid by United Brands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Republic of Honduras · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Danlí, in what is now <a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=14.03,-86.57&amp;year=1978" aria-label="Danlí on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2180 1641 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Oswaldo López Arellano"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2630 1911h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2630 1911h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=14.03,-86.57&amp;year=1978">What was here in 1978? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
